const planningBody = `<section class="section"><div class="shell approval-intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">Know the handoff</p><h2>District design review is not the County building permit.</h2><p>Brooktrails reviews the project against district standards first. Mendocino County Planning & Building Services issues the construction permit. Some projects also need County transportation or septic approval.</p></div><aside class="authority-note"><strong>Start here</strong><p>Use the Brooktrails Design Review Application before submitting plans to the County. Confirm current requirements, fees, copies, and delivery instructions with district staff.</p><a class="button" href="../${docHref('Design Review Application')}">Open Design Review Application</a></aside></div></section>
<section class="section section-tint"><div class="shell"><div class="section-intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">Your approval trail</p><h2>Seven steps, in the order they matter.</h2></div><p>Every project differs. This sequence shows who owns each decision and prevents a later-stage utility form from looking like the place to begin.</p></div><ol class="approval-trail"><li><span>01</span><div><strong>Confirm the parcel and services</strong><p>Bring the street address and assessor’s parcel number. Ask the district to confirm water and sewer availability before investing in plans.</p><a href="../contact/?topic=planning">Ask the District Desk →</a></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><strong>Prepare the district submission</strong><p>Gather the site plan, proposed work, grading and tree information, and the plan copies requested by the captured district standards.</p><a href="../${docHref('Development Standards')}">Read captured standards ↓</a></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><strong>Submit Brooktrails Design Review</strong><p>District staff and, when required, the District Architect review the project against the Brooktrails Specific Plan and district standards.</p><a href="../${docHref('Design Review Application')}">Start with the application ↓</a></div></li><li><span>04</span><div><strong>Receive written district approval</strong><p>Keep the district approval with the plans you will submit to the County. Do not begin clearing, grading, or construction based on this preview.</p></div></li><li><span>05</span><div><strong>Apply for County permits</strong><p>Mendocino County issues building permits and provides the current application, digital-submittal process, fees, and plan-review requirements.</p><a href="https://www.mendocinocounty.gov/government/planning-building-services" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open County Planning & Building Services ↗</a></div></li><li><span>06</span><div><strong>Complete additional County reviews</strong><p>A driveway or work in the public right-of-way may require a Transportation encroachment permit. An unsewered property may require Environmental Health septic review.</p><div class="inline-links"><a href="https://www.mendocinocounty.gov/departments/transportation/dot-permits-applications" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Transportation permits ↗</a><a href="https://www.mendocinocounty.gov/departments/public-health/environmental-health/land-use/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Septic and land use ↗</a></div></div></li><li><span>07</span><div><strong>Coordinate construction utilities and final inspection</strong><p>After approvals, request the current construction-water or service application directly from the district. Confirm final district inspection requirements before occupancy or permanent service.</p><a href="../contact/?topic=planning">Request current instructions →</a></div></li></ol></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="shell two-column"><div><p class="eyebrow">Reference shelf</p><h2>Use the right record at the right stage.</h2><p>The retained standards and Specific Plan materials explain the local framework. They are reference records, not proof that every fee, contact, code citation, or submission instruction remains current.</p><div class="resource-panel compact-resource-panel">${['Development Standards','Design Review Application','Chapter 20.232','Ordinance 121','Ordinance 112','2004 Specific Plan'].map(q=>{const d=findDoc(q);return d?`<a href="../${d.file}">${escapeHtml(d.title)} <span>↓</span></a>`:''}).join('')}</div><a class="text-link" href="../resources/?category=planning">Browse planning records →</a></div><aside class="privacy-stop"><p class="eyebrow">Privacy correction</p><h3>Do not email identity documents.</h3><p>The captured legacy construction-meter form requested Social Security and driver’s-license numbers. It has been removed from this preview’s public files and search because ordinary email and a public website are not secure intake channels for that information.</p><p>Request the current form and approved delivery method directly from the district.</p><a class="button button-light" href="../contact/?topic=planning">Contact the District Desk</a></aside></div></section>
<section class="section section-tint"><div class="shell story-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Long-range planning</p><h2>Growth, water & a second access road.</h2><p>The district describes its planning authority as a response to water-right and growth questions raised in the late 1980s. A second access road has remained an important planning element, with alternative-route work presented in 2009 and funding limitations reported in 2013.</p><p>Historical planning records remain available in the document center so current decisions can be read in context.</p><a class="text-link" href="../resources/?category=planning">Browse planning records →</a></div><figure class="feature-photo map-photo" id="water-system-map"><img src="../assets/images/water-system-map.jpg" alt="Map showing Brooktrails water system and tank locations"><figcaption>Water system and tank locations</figcaption></figure></div></section>`;
await write('planning/index.html',page('planning/index.html',{title:'Planning & Development',description:'Brooktrails planning, building and development review process, standards, applications, and historical planning context.',active:'services',route:'planning',eyebrow:'Planning & development',heading:'A clearer path from idea to approval.',lede:'Understand the Township and County review steps, gather the right documents, and contact staff before site work begins.',body:planningBody}));

const movingBody = `<section class="section"><div class="shell moving-compass"><div><p class="eyebrow">Before you buy or move</p><h2>Know the forest—and the systems beneath it.</h2><p>Brooktrails is a distinctive community, not a city with every service under one roof. This orientation separates what the district provides from questions owned by Mendocino County and other organizations.</p></div><aside class="moving-question"><strong>Bring one useful key</strong><p>A street address or assessor’s parcel number helps staff answer property-specific questions about district service and planning review.</p><a class="button" href="../contact/?topic=moving">Ask about a property</a></aside></div></section>
<section class="section section-tint"><div class="shell"><div class="section-intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">A practical field walk</p><h2>Seven questions worth answering first.</h2></div><p>Use this as a conversation guide, not a guarantee about a particular parcel, insurance policy, utility connection, or future approval.</p></div><div class="move-checklist"><article><span>01</span><h3>What does the district provide?</h3><p>Water, sewer, parks and conservation lands, local planning review, and district governance are the core paths presented here.</p><a href="../services/">Open Services →</a></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Can this property connect?</h3><p>Water and sewer availability can change. Confirm the exact parcel with the district before relying on a listing or captured document.</p><a href="../water/#system">Understand the utility system →</a></article><article><span>03</span><h3>What will service cost?</h3><p>Review the captured rates and fees, then confirm the current schedule and any property-specific connection or standby charges.</p><a href="../water/#billing">Review billing and rates →</a></article><article><span>04</span><h3>Can I build what I imagine?</h3><p>Brooktrails design review comes before the County permit process. Trees, grading, access, septic, and utilities can change the path.</p><a href="../planning/">Follow the approval trail →</a></article><article><span>05</span><h3>How do I prepare for wildfire?</h3><p>Use official County incident information, alerts, and evacuation-zone resources. Insurance availability and pricing must be confirmed with licensed providers.</p><a href="https://mendoready.org/plan-prepare/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open official preparedness resources ↗</a></article><article><span>06</span><h3>What is daily life like?</h3><p>Trails, redwood conservation land, gathering places, golf, water infrastructure, and local history shape the experience of Brooktrails.</p><div class="inline-links"><a href="../parks/">Explore Parks & Places →</a><a href="../history/">Discover Brooktrails →</a></div></article><article><span>07</span><h3>Who answers everything else?</h3><p>Roads, schools, taxes, waste, internet, law enforcement, building permits, and other services may belong to the County or another provider.</p><a href="../contact/?topic=moving">Start with the District Desk →</a></article></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="shell scope-map"><div><p class="eyebrow">Who owns the answer?</p><h2>A quick jurisdiction map.</h2></div><dl><div><dt>Brooktrails Township CSD</dt><dd>District water and sewer, local design review, parks and greenbelt, district records, Board and administration.</dd></div><div><dt>Mendocino County</dt><dd>Building permits, land-use and zoning review, environmental health and septic, transportation permits, property tax, and countywide emergency information.</dd></div><div><dt>Other providers</dt><dd>Schools, electric and telecommunications service, homeowners insurance, waste service, and other address-specific services.</dd></div></dl></div></section>`;
await write('moving/index.html',page('moving/index.html',{title:'Considering Brooktrails?',description:'A practical before-you-buy guide to Brooktrails services, utilities, planning, safety, recreation, and jurisdiction.',active:'history',route:'moving',eyebrow:'Considering Brooktrails?',heading:'Come for the redwoods. Check the essentials.',lede:'A practical orientation for people deciding whether a Brooktrails property and community fit the life they are planning.',body:movingBody}));

